.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBAdwWindow\fR / \fBAdwApplicationWindow\fR: fills the window with the window background (the title bar is yours: put a \fBHeaderBar\fR in).
.PP
Page surfaces: the pieces a page is built from, with \fBthe gutter in one place\fR.
.PP
Every page keeps the same distance from the window edge (\fBMetrics::gutter\fR) because nothing else in the app writes a gutter: a page is made of these. A surface that pads itself in the app is a surface that drifts: one page 12 px in, the next 16, a third that forgot. Here the number is a token (\fB[metrics] gutter\fR in the theme config, 16 px, 12 compact), so a different look changes it once.
.PP
| Surface | Use | Padding | | \-\-\- | \-\-\- | \-\-\- | | \fBscrolling\fR | a page that scrolls | the gutter on every side, inside the scrollable so the bar stays at the window edge | | \fBfull\fR | a page that does not scroll as a whole (a sheet's body) | the gutter on every side | | \fBband\fR | a section, a heading, a list header | the side gutter | | \fBtoolbar\fR | a play row, a search entry | the side gutter and a little air | | \fBrow\fR | a row of a flat list | the side gutter, so its hover surface starts on the gutter | | \fBbar_padding\fR | the padding of a bar (a player bar) | the side gutter and a little air |
.PP
They are all a \fBContainer\fR (fluid) with the right padding, so a surface is a container too. Enforce the rule with \fBcargo xtask lint\-gutters\fR.
.PP
.nf
